From: Takoserver Native source candidate
Subject: [SOURCE ONLY v6.12] retain original origins before positive skb_split effects

Apply after the retained formal22 source graph. Before managed-zcopy page
references or either split helper can move payload, retain the original
origin union on the actual receiving header with the existing merge helper.
Only len < original skb->len transfers positive tail payload; zero-tail has
no new origin effect. All original statements, gfp0 zerocopy preconditions,
page/protocol behavior and sticky failure poison remain unchanged. CONFIG-off
removes this addition. No new API/helper/state. No saved actual caller, fixed
OCI/TCP reachability, physical page/net lastfree, fulltraffic or terminal
qualification is claimed by this generic source retention contract.

diff --git a/net/core/skbuff.c b/net/core/skbuff.c
--- a/net/core/skbuff.c
+++ b/net/core/skbuff.c
@@ -4254,6 +4254,14 @@
 	int pos = skb_headlen(skb);
 	const int zc_flags = SKBFL_SHARED_FRAG | SKBFL_PURE_ZEROCOPY;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_TAKO_TERMINAL
+	/* Retain the original history before downgrade can acquire page refs
+	 * and before either split helper moves payload to the other header.
+	 */
+	if (len < skb->len)
+		tako_terminal_skb_merge(skb1, skb);
+#endif
+
 	skb_zcopy_downgrade_managed(skb);
 
 	skb_shinfo(skb1)->flags |= skb_shinfo(skb)->flags & zc_flags;
